, Open"]] [:script {} "$('#same_games_select').change(function(){location.href='/results/' + $('#same_games_select').val();})"]] " | " [:form {:class "form-inline form-inline-header"} [:span {} "Not held in other editions"]] " | " [:a {:href "/event_names/277"} "Event type"]] [:h1 {:class "event_title"} "High Jump, Open" [:small {}]] [:table {:class "biodata"} [:tbody {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Date"] [:td {} " 2 June 1900 — 16:30"]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Status"] [:td {} "Olympic"]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Location"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/venues/196"} "Place de Breteuil, Paris"]]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Participants"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/events/185001"} "11 from 4 countries"]]]]] [:div {:class "description"} [:p {} "The high jump used to be a common competition but was rarely held later in the 20th century. There were 18 entrants in this event, with 14 starters, although we have not been able to identify all starters. The competition started at 1.20 metres, and initially advanced by 10 cm increments. All competitors cleared through 1.50 metres. The horses and riders were allowed three attempts at each successive height, as with human high jumping. The 1900 Olympic title was shared at 1.85 metres by Italian " [:a {:href "/athletes/12871"} "Giangiorgio, Count Trissino"] " aboard " [:em {} [:a {:href "/horses/1823"} "Oreste"]] ", and Frenchman " [:a {:href "/athletes/12006"} "Alfred Gardère"] ", who rode " [:em {} [:a {:href "/horses/380"} "Canéla"]] " (owned by Count Oscar Heeren). Riding a different horse, " [:em {} [:a {:href "/horses/1623"} "Melopo"]] ", Trissino also finished fourth in this event. There was a jump-off to decide the third and fourth places between Count Trissino and " [:a {:href "/athletes/12902"} "Georges Van De Poele"] ", aboard " [:em {} [:a {:href "/horses/3377"} "Ludlow"]] "."] "\n\n" [:p {} "The best on record in this era was 2.40 metres, set by " [:em {} "Heatherbloom"] ", ridden by Dick Donnelly at Richmond, Virginia, in 1902, although " [:em {} "Heatherbloom"] " and Donnelly had unofficial marks in 1902 of 2.49 and 2.515 metres. However, the first recognized " [:a {:href "/organizations/58"} "FEI (Fédération Équestre Internationale)"] " high jump record was 2.35 metres by " [:em {} "Conspirateur"] ", ridden by Captain Crousse (FRA) at the Grand Palais, in Paris, on 12 April 1906. The final FEI-recognized high jump record in the 20th century was 2.47 metres by " [:em {} "Huaso"] ", ridden by Alberto Larraguibel Morales at an international show in Santiago, Chile, on 5 February 1949."] "\n\n" [:p {} "A more modern variant of this event is now contested, termed the " [:em {} "puissance"] ". It is also a high jump event but with some differences in the details of the fences and the competition. The current indoor record for " [:em {} "puissance"] " is held by German rider " [:a {:href "/athletes/12756"} "Franke Sloothaak"] ", who, in June 1991, jumped 2.40 metres in Chaudfontaine, Belgium, riding " [:em {} "Optiebeurs Golo"] "."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "Horse"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "Distance"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "=1"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/12871"} "Giangiorgio, Conte Trissino"]] [:td {} [:i {} [:a {:href "/horses/1823"} "Oreste"]]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/ITA"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/ITA.png"}] "ITA"]] [:td {} "1.85"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "=1"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/12006"} "Alfred Gardère"]] [:td {} [:i {} [:a {:href "/horses/380"} "Canéla"]]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/FRA"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/FRA.png"}] "FRA"]] [:td {} "1.85"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr